
ML = finding patterns in numbers

Way of working: Numbers → Vectors  →  Matrices

Scalar = simple one number. Ex. 1, 2, 7, 8
Vector = ordered collection of numbers. Ex. [3,4], [5,2,7], [2,7,9,12,15]
(Single number inside it is called component)

Visualization: normal cartesian method, diff for 1D, 2D, 3D, 4D,....



USE OF VECTORS IN ML:
Ex. Iris flower 

Features :
Sepal Length
Sepal Width
Petal Length
Petal Width

Flower measurement: 
5.1
3.5
1.4
0.2

Flower measurement in vectorial form: [5.1, 3.5, 1.4, 0.2]  ← Feature Vector



Everything becomes vector:
Images → Millions of numbers
Text → Word vectors
Audio → Signal vectors
Video → Huge vectors
Everything becomes numbers


Ex. movie recommandation. Similar movies will have similar vectors (close vectors). Then a closer vector movie will be recommended. 



LENGTH(MAGNITUDE OF VECTOR):
Under root of the sum of the square of components of the vector

Ex. triangle with sides [3, 4, 5] → Magnitude: √ (3²  + 4²  + 5²) 
For [a₁,a₂,...,aₙ] → Mgnituude: √(a₁²+a₂²+...+aₙ²)

Written as: ||A||

Called: the norm of the vector 



Vector1: [a1, a2, a3]
Vector2: [b1, b2, b3]
Distance between vector 1 and 2: √ ((a1 - b1)² + (a2 - b2)²  + (a3 - b3)² )
How far these vectors are

Use of distance between two vectors: ex. For recommendation systems, less distance more similar




SCALAR OPERATATIONS: 
Adding 5 into [2, 3] → [7, 8]
Same for +, -, /, *

Dot product: Vector A · Vector B = [x1*x2 + y1*y2] ← Scalar ans

To measure angle between vectors (Direction measurement) : cosθ=∣A∣∣B∣ / A⋅B​ 






